                <pb facs="0837" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg751"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that he has impressively informed the Turkish minister of the
                    displeasure and amazement of the President at the manner in which his minister’s
                    request for an audience with the Sultan has been treated.)</p>
            </div>
